--- rendered ---
error[E-unit]: dB levels can't be used in arithmetic here
  --> value_arith.spl:5:44
  |
5 |     let r1 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 2 * 3dB };
  |                                            ^^^^^^^ not a plain quantity

error[E-unit]: expected `Ω` (a resistance), found a temperature
  --> value_arith.spl:6:44
  |
6 |     let r2 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: -(10°C) };
  |                                            ^^^^^^^ this is a temperature

error[E-value]: division by zero
  --> value_arith.spl:8:49
  |
8 |     let r3 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1k / 0 };
  |                                                 ^ the divisor is zero

error[E-value]: division by zero
  --> value_arith.spl:9:56
  |
9 |     let r4 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: (1k ± 1%) / (2 - 2) };
  |                                                        ^^^^^^^ the divisor is zero

error[E-value]: a tolerance can't be negative
   --> value_arith.spl:11:49
   |
11 |     let r5 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1k ± -1% };
   |                                                 ^^^ `±` already means both directions

error[E-value]: a tolerance can't be negative
   --> value_arith.spl:12:49
   |
12 |     let r6 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1k ± -(50) };
   |                                                 ^^^^^ `±` already means both directions

error[E-value]: a tolerance or range can only be scaled
   --> value_arith.spl:14:45
   |
14 |     let r7 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: (1k ± 1%) + 1k };
   |                                             ^^^^^^^ compute the nominal first, then add the spread
   |
   = note: `2 * (1k ± 1%)` works; adding to a spread doesn't

error[E-value]: a tolerance or range can only be scaled
   --> value_arith.spl:15:44
   |
15 |     let r8 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 1k / (2 ± 1%) };
   |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compute the nominal first, then add the spread
   |
   = note: `2 * (1k ± 1%)` works; adding to a spread doesn't

error[E-value]: a tolerance or range can only be scaled
   --> value_arith.spl:16:44
   |
16 |     let r9 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: (1k ± 1%) * 1V };
   |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ compute the nominal first, then add the spread
   |
   = note: `2 * (1k ± 1%)` works; adding to a spread doesn't

error[E-unit]: can't add a plain number and a ratio
   --> value_arith.spl:18:45
   |
18 |     let r10 = Resistor { a: p, b: n, value: 100 + 5% };
   |                                             ^^^^^^^^ different units

error[E-value]: `rating` takes an exact value
   --> value_arith.spl:20:58
   |
20 |     let c1 = Capacitor { a: p, b: n, value: 1u, rating: (25V ± 1V) };
   |                                                          ^^^^^^^^ a tolerance or range
